<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<subsection xml:id="make-up_policy">
  <title>Make-up Policy</title>
  <p component="exams">
    If you know in advance that you will be absent for a University-excused reason, you must arrange to take the exam before you leave.
    In the case of an emergency, you must contact me to schedule a make-up exam within three class days of returning.
  </p>

  <p component="quizzes">
    No makeup quizzes will be given.
    Instead, your two lowest quiz scores <ndash/> including a zero for any missed quiz <ndash/> are automatically dropped when your final grade is calculated.
    The only exception is a documented, University-excused absence beyond these two drops, as described in the Attendance Policy.
  </p>

  <!-- <p> -->
  <!--   Make-up opportunities will only be granted in cases of documented emergencies or university-approved absences (e.g., illness, family emergencies, or official university activities). -->
  <!--     Except in extraordinary circumstances, students must notify the instructor before the missed deadline or class. -->
  <!--     Students who need to make up work due to a University-related activity requiring an absence from class must arrange for work to be completed <alert>before</alert> leaving.  -->
  <!-- </p> -->
</subsection>
